d":"18 Via Po"},{"n":"Supermarket","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":44.499241,"lo":12.278169,"d":1037,"h":"07:00-13:00,16:00-20:00","f":["wc"]},{"n":"San Giovanni Battista, Ravenna","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.420571,"lo":12.20124,"d":9933,"ds":"San Giovanni Battista is a baroque church in the historic center of Ravenna, Italy, built in 1689 by Pietro Grossi. The church here, a three-nave basilica, was built in the 6th century. In 1688, it was strongly damaged by an earthquake, demolished, and a new building was constructed in the same place.","wpu":"San Giovanni Battista, Ravenna","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Ravenna_SanGiovanniBattista_0055.JPG/960px-Ravenna_SanGiovanniBattista_0055.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Giovanni Evangelista, Ravenna","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.417904,"lo":12.205526,"d":9960,"ds":"San Giovanni Evangelista is a church in Ravenna, Italy. It was built in the fifth century AD by the Roman imperial princess Galla Placidia \"in fulfilment of a vow made by her to S. John Evangelist, when, on her way from Constantinople to Ravenna, she was in danger of shipwreck.","wpu":"San Giovanni Evangelista, Ravenna","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cc/Ravenna_1978_037.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Ravenna ( rə-VEN-ə; Italian: [raˈvenna], also locally [raˈvɛn(n)a] ; Romagnol: Ravèna, Ravêna) is the capital city of the Province of Ravenna, in the Emilia-Romagna region of Northern Italy. It was the capital city of the Western Roman Empire during the fifth century AD until its collapse in 476, after which it served as the capital of the Ostrogothic Kingdom and then the Byzantine Exarchate of Ravenna. With a population of 156,475 inhabitants as of 2026, it is the 24th-largest city in Italy.","wpu":"Ravenna","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Ravenna_Mausoleo_di_Teodorico_Esterno_08.jpg/960px-Ravenna_Mausoleo_di_Teodorico_Esterno_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}